  "entries": [
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 2,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 2,
      "title": "",
      "content": "prophet, (c-8) Many read 'in the prophets.' My impression is that it was originally 'in the prophet' simply. way. (d-21) Mal. 3.1."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 3,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 3,
      "title": "",
      "content": "straight. (e-17) Isa. 40.3."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 13,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 13,
      "title": "",
      "content": "ministered (a-21) As Matt. 4.11, diakoneo."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 15,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 15,
      "title": "",
      "content": "in (b-18) 'Believe in,' &c. A rare form of expression. It refers to believing, in the truth of the substance of a thing. see 2Tim. 1.12."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 18,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 18,
      "title": "",
      "content": "trawl-nets (c-5) See Note, Matt. 4.20."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 23,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 23,
      "title": "",
      "content": "by (d-10) En. see Matt. 3.11, Note c. Not merely he had one, but he was completely under its power, characterized by it."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 24,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 24,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Eh! (e-2) The imperative of the verb 'to let alone,' but used as an interjection, as a cry of dissatisfaction. Nazarene? (f-11) The force of 'Nazarene' here is simply, I apprehend, 'of Nazareth.' The word is different from that translated 'Nazaraean' in Matt. 2.23 and elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 34,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 34,
      "title": "",
      "content": "knew (a-25) Oida. had the inward consciousness of who he was. see Note, 1Cor. 8.1."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 41,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 41,
      "title": "",
      "content": "touched (b-11) 'To touch freely,' 'handle,' as Matt. 8.3."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 45,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 45,
      "title": "",
      "content": "came (c-36) The imperfect tense, 'were, or kept, coming to him.'"
    },
    {
