      "end_verse": 21,
      "title": "",
      "content": "new (a-7) Lit. 'unfulled' or 'unmilled,' as Matt. 9.16."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 26,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 26,
      "title": "",
      "content": "of] (b-12) i.e. in the section of a book in which the fact is recorded."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 3,
      "start_verse": 5,
      "end_chapter": 3,
      "end_verse": 5,
      "title": "",
      "content": "distressed (c-8) The Greek word is found here only. It is questioned whether it means 'sympathizing grief' (as LXX, Ps. 69.20;) or 'deep grief.' There is, I apprehend, sorrow for, with an intensive force in it; not sympathy, which is feeling with, but feeling what a state they were in, with grief for it."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 3,
      "start_verse": 6,
      "end_chapter": 3,
      "end_verse": 6,
      "title": "",
      "content": "counsel (d-11) The word is used also for a council, Acts 25.12. It may be more in this sense here, but a private one."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 3,
      "start_verse": 13,
      "end_chapter": 3,
      "end_verse": 13,
      "title": "",
      "content": "mountain, (a-7) The mountain in contrast with the plain. see Note, Matt. 5.1."
    },
